  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary of results (see the report for details)\n- Conventions verified: t1,t2,t3 mutually commute and t4 is a scalar (both diagonal and companion frames, qmin columns at u-(k-1)h).\n- Dimensions (words t_a(theta_{1,2}+mh)^{+-1}, a=1..3, m=-4..4, products of up to 2 factors; 102 allowed factors): R1 exact and mod p: dim S = 54, dim S12 = 6 (basis: matrix units E11, E14, E41, E44, E22, E33 in x[A,F]); singles-only gives the same S12. R2 (mod p): dim S = 256, dim S12 = 16 (no constraint). R3 (mod p): dim S = 9, dim S12 = 3. Exact R2/R3 runs were not completed (too slow); R3 targets were not tested.\n- On R1 every common-rotation target T_A..T_D and every mixed piece / power of Lambda lies in S12 (membership table above), but this is a degeneracy of R1: v and u are supported on the indices {1,4}, so any diagonal rotation acts on them as a degree-1 polynomial in Lambda.\n- One-point generating functions: no genuine 3-term combination (all of c1,c2,c3 nonzero from non-localising words) exists for shifts in -3h..3h; every localising combination is a combination of individually localising single words. 1 - kappa t1(theta2) is localised on R1 but not a product (rank 4).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
